abstract: >
  An open reproducible benchmark for multi-crop yield prediction spanning
  ten crops × 401 German NUTS-3 districts × 21 years of harmonized DWD
  weather, MODIS satellite, SoilGrids soil, and Destatis yield data
  (2003–2023). Six deep-learning architectures (XGBoost, DLinear, LSTM,
  PatchTST, iTransformer, TFT) are evaluated head-to-head with cross-model
  fusion methods, and a first-principles crop-model compatibility taxonomy
  predicts per-crop model choice from crop biology and model inductive
  biases (top-1 hit rate 90%, Spearman ρ = 0.69). Climate stress test
  under CMIP6 SSP scenarios (EC-Earth3-CC, MPI-ESM1-2-LR) via delta-method
  counterfactuals.
